.TH LINUXPODS 1 "April 2026" "linuxpods 1.0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linuxpods \- command-line control tool for LinuxPods
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linuxpods
.I COMMAND
.br
.B linuxpods \-h\fR|\fB\-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B linuxpods
is a small command-line client that talks to a running
.BR linuxpods-daemon (1)
over a local socket. It is intended for scripting, debugging and headless use
where the Plasma 6 widget is not available.
.PP
All commands operate on the currently-connected AirPods device.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B noise:off
Disable noise control.
.TP
.B noise:anc
Enable Active Noise Cancellation.
.TP
.B noise:transparency
Enable Transparency mode.
.TP
.B noise:adaptive
Enable Adaptive mode on supported devices.
.TP
.B ca:on
Enable Conversational Awareness.
.TP
.B ca:off
Disable Conversational Awareness.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h , \-\-help
Print usage and available commands, then exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B linuxpods
exits with status 1 when invoked without arguments or when it cannot
connect to the daemon, and status 0 after displaying help or submitting
a command. The socket protocol is one-way: a zero status does not confirm
that AirPods are connected, that the command was recognized, or that the
requested setting was applied.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/linuxpods-daemon
Per-user command socket created by the daemon.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR linuxpods-daemon (1),
.BR busctl (1)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at
.UR https://github.com/Explor3Universe/LinuxPods/issues
.UE .
